* sg13cmos5l-bandgap -- closed-loop vref temperature-sweep bench body (issue #30, Part of #5).
* Template: sim/grid-run.sh substitutes @@VDD@@ and @@WORK@@ and writes the deck to
* sim/build/closed-loop-vref-pvt-boxtc/deck.cir. The model `.lib` cards and the supply
* value come from the `klt sim` request (request-grid.json).
*
* Same fixture as sim/closed-loop-vref-pvt/vref.cir.tmpl -- a DC supply, vss at 0, and the
* substrate net `sub!` tied to vss through a 0 V source -- with ONE difference: there is no
* 2 ms transient here. The analysis is a DC sweep of TEMP (`dc temp -40 125 1`, 166 points),
* so the whole -40...125 C characteristic is solved INSIDE one corner unit and the
* temperature-coefficient reduction over it is a `klt sim` measurement rather than a
* post-hoc reduction across units. `klt sim` has no cross-corner reduction, so a
* temperature AXIS could not express a ppm/C figure at all.
*
* The DC operating point is the correct, non-degenerate closed-loop solution for this
* circuit, not the zero state: measured at this PDK pin, `dc temp` returns vref = 1.19746 V
* at 7.14 C and 1.19093 V at 125 C on typ/3.30 V, continuous with the transient bench's
* settled 1.19696 V at 27 C (sim/closed-loop-vref-pvt, decision record 0009). That
* continuity is what licenses a DC analysis here; it is re-checked by this bench's own
* vref_27_v measurement, whose plausible_range fails a degenerate solve rather than
* recording it as a characteristic.
*
* OSDI objects load through the request's options.osdi_preload, not a .control block: a
* .control block here would land inside the deck `klt sim` `.include`s, not in the top deck
* it generates, so its commands would never run.
*
* NO SPICE TITLE LINE (issue #19): `klt sim` `.include`s this deck into a top deck of its
* own, so line 1 here is not in title position and a title line would be parsed as a
* netlist element. Every line of this template is a comment or a card, and grid-run.sh
* writes its own leading `*` line as well.

* rshunt/gmin: convergence aids only, far below any current read here (same values the
* source closed-loop bench and sim/closed-loop-vref-pvt use).
.options rshunt=1e9 gmin=1e-9

Vvdd vdd 0 dc @@VDD@@
Vvss vss 0 dc 0
Vsub sub! vss dc 0

.include "@@WORK@@/bandgap_top.spice"
